{"post": true, "caption": "Risking 1% doesn't mean buying 1% of your account. It means that if your stop-loss hits, you lose about 1%.\nThe simple formula: position size = money you risk ÷ distance to your stop.\n$1,000 account, $10 risk, stop 2% away: a $500 position. Stop 5% away: $200. Fees and fast markets can make the real loss a bit bigger.\nDid you know this? Yes or no.\n\nEducation only. Not financial advice.\n\n#CandleAndCode #TradingForBeginners #Risk101 #PositionSizing #RiskManagement", "tag": "RISK 101", "footer": "Education only. Not financial advice.", "bpm": 100, "scenes": [{"type": "hook", "dur": 2.4, "size": 140, "lines": [{"t": "RISK $10.", "c": "red"}, {"t": "BUY $500.", "c": "green"}]}, {"type": "text", "dur": 2.8, "size": 88, "lines": [{"t": "Sounds wrong?", "c": "fg"}, {"t": "It's position sizing.", "c": "green"}, {"t": "Watch the math.", "c": "muted"}]}, {"type": "text", "dur": 3.0, "size": 88, "lines": [{"t": "$1,000 account.", "c": "fg"}, {"t": "Risk 1% a trade.", "c": "fg"}, {"t": "That's $10.", "c": "green"}]}, {"type": "text", "dur": 3.2, "size": 88, "lines": [{"t": "Your stop-loss", "c": "fg"}, {"t": "sets your size.", "c": "green"}, {"t": "Not your mood.", "c": "muted"}]}, {"type": "stat", "dur": 3.0, "size": 170, "label": "Risk ÷ distance to your stop", "value": "$10 ÷ 2%", "note": "= a $500 position.", "c": "green"}, {"type": "bars", "dur": 6.0, "title": "Same $10 at risk", "subtitle": "position size, before fees", "rows": [{"l": "Stop 2% away", "v": 500, "vl": "$500", "lc": "fg", "bc": "green"}, {"l": "Stop 5% away", "v": 200, "vl": "$200", "lc": "fg", "bc": "green"}, {"l": "Stop 10% away", "v": 100, "vl": "$100", "lc": "fg", "bc": "green"}]}, {"type": "text", "dur": 3.0, "size": 92, "lines": [{"t": "Wider stop?", "c": "fg"}, {"t": "Smaller size.", "c": "fg"}, {"t": "Same $10 loss.", "c": "green"}]}, {"type": "text", "dur": 3.2, "size": 96, "lines": [{"t": "Size from risk,", "c": "fg"}, {"t": "not from hope.", "c": "green"}]}, {"type": "end", "dur": 2.2, "line": "Trade with a system, not a feeling."}]}
